# The tree is stored as LF, everywhere, on purpose: tools/fetch-thaumaturge.sh is run directly by
# CI and by Linux and macOS builders, and a checkout that hands it CRLF line endings stops at the
# first line with a "not found" that names no file. Keeping one ending for the whole tree also means
# the working folder and the committed bytes agree, which is what the byte-for-byte comparisons in
# this repository rely on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled artifacts carry bytes that no line-ending rule may touch.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
